+# TF-spark: the deployed TF-opt tree + SparkFold `spark-exl3`
+
+Branch `spark-port` of `~/data/runs/tfdev/TF-spark`. Commits, oldest first:
+
+1. `044f872` TF-opt as deployed 2026-10-10 (the baseline; 0.6.5 + my EXL3 prompt kernel, special-token escape, tool-call slip fixes, `TENSORFOLD_PIN_EXTRA_GIB`).
+2. `ef1ffcd` merge of `grearjake-star/TensorFold@806b345` (SparkFold, 89 commits on the same 0.6.5 base `609ca41`).
+3. `29bc26e` + later: the prefix-miss reason log, the lone-stream graph state in the startup log, tests following `call_name`.
+
+## How the merge was resolved (10 conflicting files)
+
+| Files | Taken | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| `cuda/exl3/experts.{cpp,cu,py}`, `experts_cb{0,1,2}.cu`, `forward.py`, `exl3_pack.py`, `exl3.py` | SparkFold | Its `experts_prompt.cuh` does what my `grouped_mb` did (decode a weight tile once, reuse it for the item's 64 pairs) and claims the same bits as the grouping kernel; it also brings plan items, the side stream, wider windows. My kernel is kept OUTSIDE the tree (`../mb-kernel-opt/`) for a bit-oracle comparison. |
+| `cuda/reply_text.py` | SparkFold's `call_name` | It sends a call to an undeclared tool under its own name in single- and multi-call modes (my `keep_unknown` did it for multi-call only). My `collapse_call_openers` stays. |
+| `cuda/server.py` | both | `PreparedRequest` carries `defused` (mine) and `effort`/`request_id` (theirs); the final-answer path keeps my restore/collapse/undeclared-tool warning and uses their `policy.parsed_content`. |
+
+Not touched by the conflicts and still in place: `server/prompts.py` (special-token escape), `TENSORFOLD_PIN_EXTRA_GIB` in `engine.py`, my three test files (one assertion changed with `call_name`).
+
+## What the merge brings (all env knobs; defaults are the tree's, see the start script profiles)
+
+- Prefix/kept-state policy: `TF_KEEP`, slot choice (`_claim`, `_cheapest_idle`, `TF_FRESH_SLACK`), system-block checkpoint (`TF_SYS_CHECKPOINT`), warm starts (`TF_WARM_STARTS`).
+- CUDA graphs: per-slot lone-stream graphs, `TF_SOLO_ROWS` (pre-size the graph slot and capture every context bucket at start; issue #336), no `gc.collect` per capture, shared-round graphs (`TF_MULTI_GRAPHS`, default on).
+- Prefill: `TF_EXL3_PROMPT=prompt` kernel, `TENSORFOLD_PREFILL_ROWS`/`TF_EXL3_MOE_WINDOW` up to 4096, fused fp16 prompt matmuls, tall tiles (`TF_EXL3_TALL`), HC read-out fusion, QSA prompt indexer, shared expert on a side stream (`TF_EXL3_PROMPT_SIDE`).
+- Decode: n-gram stage batching and read-ahead (`TF_STAGE_BATCH`, `TF_DECODE_AHEAD`, `TF_NGRAM_AHEAD`), fused MoE routing (`TF_MOE_ROUTE_FUSED`), expected-time draft stop (`TF_DRAFT_COST`, default 0.06 tokens/ms), joint draft pricing (`TF_JOINT_PRICE`, off), trained MTP head loader (`TF_MTP_HEAD`, no weights).
+- Off by default and NOT to be switched on without a quality check: `TF_EXL3_HC_FP8=1` (changes output bits).
+- Server: `/v1/models` `context_length`, `--name-priority`, TPOT histogram, request-end reasons, think-tag handling, open-file limit.
+
+Added here: `prefixes.miss_note` (log line `prefix miss: ... diverges at token N of the M-token kept state` or `no kept state`; `TF_MISS_NOTE=0` off), and the startup line for lone-stream graphs.
+
+## Tests
+
+- CPU (`bin/cpu_pytest.sh`, no GPU): 3,591 passed, 55 skipped (pure SparkFold: 3,567 passed; the difference is my tests). Residency tests need `--ulimit memlock=-1`.
+- Extensions compiled in this image (CUDA 13.3, sm_121): `tensorfold_exl3_experts_v8r` 112 s, `tensorfold_exl3_linear_v4` 58 s, `tensorfold_qwen4_exp_qsa_prompt_p7` 9 s, into `~/.cache/tensorfold-spark`.
+- GPU tests share the live server's GPU, so the memory gate has almost no room: with `TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB=2 TENSORFOLD_CUDA_MEMORY_LIMIT_GB=3` the same 7 tests + 2 errors (growth past first rows, shared-round graphs) fail on merged and on pure SparkFold alike; they need the server stopped.
+
+## Serving
+
+`~/data/runs/llm/start-qwen38-flash-next-exl3-spark.sh` (PROFILE=safe|spark|bare). Rollback: `~/data/runs/llm/start-qwen38-flash-next-exl3-tf.sh` (TF-opt sources, `~/.cache/tensorfold-v065`).
